e franchise  through event tv shows on disney plus  this meant that the boba fett movie was  once again kicked to the curb eventually  fett would make his way into disney's  star wars galaxy in the second season of  the mandalorian and his own series the  book of boba fett  i'm a simple man making his way through  the galaxy  like my father before me at the start of  the 2010s it looked like theatrical 3d  re-releases of classic movies were about  to become a big thing with the original  lion king becoming a surprise hit when  it was released in 3d in september 2011  the stage seemed set for a series of  subsequent 3d re-releases to make a  similar killing at the box office these  included the phantom menace 3d which was  planned as the start of an ambitious  push to re-release all six original star  wars movies in a whole new dimension  sadly the phantom menace 3d didn't  exactly blow the doors off the box  office sure its worldwide gross wasn't  enough to push the movie's lifetime haul  past the one billion dollar threshold  but that was its only accomplishment  after a decent opening weekend the movie  made just less than half of what the  lion king 3d had accumulated at the  domestic box office autumn 2013 release  dates were set for 3d re-releases of the  other two star wars prequel films but  they were eventually pulled after disney  bought lucasfilm as a result the  studio's ambitious plans have been left  unrealized  today star wars the clone wars is known  as a tv show that took major risks by  focusing on unsung supporting characters  in the franchise and even exploring some  outright esoteric concepts but you have  to walk before you can run and most  animated programs begin their runs with  more awkward episodes rarely though do  these more imperfect episodes play out  on the big screen but such was the case  for the theatrical film star wars the  clone wars released in 2008 the clone  wars was meant to serve as a feature  linked pilot for the series however the  film's animation style could never hope  to compete with the kind of visuals seen  in its big budget competitors worse this  movie utilized a more juvenile sense of  humor and dialogue that later seasons of  the clone wars would jettison all in all  the whole project was quite poorly  thought out and it didn't even bring in  much money for the studio cementing the  project as an underwhelming beginning to  a beloved tv series  george lucas got along so well with the  team behind the trio of robot chicken  star wars specials that he assembled the  same group in the late 2000s for a new  sci-fi project uh as the creator of uh  mara jade  wait  i am not the creator of our jade and i  want you to get out of this office right  now this was star wars detours an  animated tv show that would take a  satirical spin on many of the series  beloved characters clips of the program  were shown at star wars celebration in  2012 and included such antics as obi-wan  kenobi becoming a comedian and admiral  akbar failing to think of the word trap  just two months after the world  discovered detours however disney bought  lucasfilm and the whole landscape of  star wars entertainment changed forever  disney had its own plans for the  franchise of course and none of them  revolved around detours even though  around 40 episodes of the show had been  completed the program was shelved seth  green later confirmed that lucasfilm's  new management just didn't see the show  fitting in with their more  serious-minded plans for the franchise  rumors continue to persist that detours  will eventually drop on disney plus in  the near future but otherwise this  particular project seems to have totally  fizzled out ted i got your vouchers  out  there i'm sorry about that i'm so sorry  lego and star wars have turned out to be  a match made in heaven the two pop  culture properties have been working  together for decades now on everything  from toys to video games to movies so  why shouldn't there eventually be plans  to turn lego star wars into an ongoing  tv show well such a creative endeavor  once emerged through the freemaker  adventures which followed a trio of  siblings who get swept up in the greater  battle between the rebel alliance and  the galactic empire to date this show is  the only instance of a lego star wars  property scoring an ongoing tv program  in a traditional seasonal format with  most other televised lego star wars  properties emerging as either tv  specials or miniseries and given that  the freemaker adventures didn't set the  world on fire that's not surprising  either the show wasn't exactly a massive  flop but it was nowhere near as  impactful as lucasfilm's other animated  shows and it didn't attract the kind of  fan base that the lego star wars video  games have in the end the show lasted  only two seasons  originally the next step for the star  wars franchise after revenge of the sith  wasn't a sequel trilogy but a foray into  the world of television the clone wars  was to begin airing in 2008 and then a  live-action star wars tv show later  named star wars underworld would debut  shortly thereafter the program was set  to explore all kinds of nooks and  crannies of the galaxy far far away it  would cover everything from how han and  chewie met to the origin story of  palpatine the series had grand ambitions  indeed and was personally overseen by  george lucas but underworld never got  off the ground for one simple reason  money the financial strain required to  pull off a production of this scale on a  network tv budget proved too massive to  overcome lucasfilm executive pablo  hidalgo later noted that george lucas  was unable to expand his grady ranch  property to accommodate sound stages  which also forced the show's production  to ground to a halt nowadays shows such  as the mandalorian have made star wars  television practically commonplace in  that sense perhaps star wars underworld  was simply a project ahead of its 